fixture parry_window_connecting_first_frame
doc BUILD.md s6 Parry (ADR-0013, the window counts world ticks): a press on the window's first frame, 7 frames before the landing, parries even when the press itself connects with the telegraphing dummy. The press is attack facing the dummy, so its strike hits and its 2 f of hitstop must not stretch the 8 f window ("the 8 frames that end on the frame it lands"). The swing lands on frame 53.
room test/dummy_swing
frames 80
input
  46 R attack
end
expect
  at 53 event.parry=1 event.player_hit=0 hearts=5
  never 0..79 event.player_hit=1
end
